# The annotations of the 128K glue as it runs at $5B00-$5BE2 (227 bytes, block 2's $61B6-$6298, copied there by
# block 2's set-up on a 128K): the single source of src/game/glue*.asm (tools/part_mkasm.py). The image is
# work/parts/glue-5b00.bin; the code is what the analysis builds work/stage2/glue (the set-up, frames 3302-3314) and
# work/stage2/game (play, 3313:51573-13702) ran, widened by mkgame's walk. The 48K game's addresses it patches are
# named here after what the 48K code does there (work/stage1/dis/game48-static.asm).

@equ $7F7C PauseState ; the game's variable the routine at $B197 ends by setting to 4 (LD ($7F7C),A at $B1B0)
@equ $7F96 IntFlag ; the game's variable its interrupt handler at $A9E4 sets ($80)
@equ $858B ClearScreen ; the game's routine: the attributes and the border cleared (from $858E)
@equ $A581 IntTailSite 4 ; the game's handler tail POP BC: POP DE: POP HL (its POP AF at $A584 stays)
@equ $A584 IntTailRest ; the POP AF after it
@equ $A620 ClearSite1 2 ; a CALL ClearScreen's operand (the routine before $A623)
@equ $A7F3 ClearSite2 2 ; a CALL ClearScreen's operand (the game-over routine before $A7F7)
@equ $A9E5 IntMenuSite 3 ; LD HL,IntFlag in the game's interrupt handler at $A9E4
@equ $A9F7 IntPlaySite 4 ; PUSH IX: PUSH IY at the start of the game's main interrupt work
@equ $A9FB IntPlayRest ; the instruction after them
@equ $AB03 IntEndSite 4 ; POP IY: POP IX at the end of that work
@equ $AB07 IntEndRest ; the instruction after them
@equ $ABDC Key4Site 2 ; the operand of CALL Z,$B197 (key 4, row $F7FE bit 3, in the play loop)
@equ $AD56 LevelSetUp ; the game's routine $B023 called first (it copies a level record to $81D7)
@equ $AFB4 ClearSite3 2 ; a CALL ClearScreen's operand (in $AFB0, which the main loop calls at $B200)
@equ $B024 LevelSite 2 ; the operand of CALL LevelSetUp at $B023 (the start of a game's level)
@equ $B197 Key4Routine ; the game's routine key 4 calls (it ends at $B1B3, after a wait)
@equ $B1B0 Key4End 3 ; LD (PauseState),A at its end
@equ $B201 MainLoopCall 2 ; the operand of the main loop's CALL $AFB0 at $B200
@equ $B2F0 BeeperSound ; the 48K's RequestEffect (A = the beeper effect, 1-6): RET on 128K
@equ $B30C BeeperPlay ; the 48K's EffectPlay (the beeper effect player, a main-loop job): RET on 128K
@equ $B30D HookSound ; the shared hook stub (src/game/stubs.asm)
@equ $B446 BeeperTone ; the DI of TitleTune, the 48K's beeper title tune: a NOP on 128K
@const PAGE4 $14 ; $7FFD: bank 4 at $C000 (the engine), the 48 BASIC ROM, screen 0
@const PAGE0 $10 ; $7FFD: bank 0 at $C000 (the game)
@const PORT_7FFD $7FFD ; the 128K paging port
@const EngineMusicOn $C968 ; the engine (page 4, src/sound/engine.asm): start the music
@const EngineMusicOff $C96B ; stop the music
@const EnginePlay $C96E ; one step of the music and the effects
@isub $5B08 LD A,PAGE4
@isub $5B0A LD BC,PORT_7FFD
@isub $5B0F CALL EnginePlay
@isub $5B12 LD A,PAGE0
@isub $5B14 LD BC,PORT_7FFD
@isub $5B54 LD A,PAGE4
@isub $5B56 LD BC,PORT_7FFD
@isub $5B5B CALL EngineMusicOff
@isub $5B61 CALL NZ,EngineMusicOn
@isub $5B64 LD A,PAGE0
@isub $5B66 LD BC,PORT_7FFD

@module glue ; the 128K glue: the engine each frame, the music on and off, the patches
@about GlueInstall, called once by block 2's set-up on a 128K, writes the patches; the rest is what they reach. The game's interrupt handlers now call FramePlay through one of four small entries, which each do the instructions their patch overwrote: the engine plays one step from page 4. The menus' handlers step it once an interrupt, every TV frame; the play handler twice a pass, and a pass takes two TV frames (the next interrupt is lost under DI), so the engine steps once a TV frame on average in play too (docs/09-sound.md 9.8). The music is started after each screen clear the game does at its menus (ClearThenMusic, MusicOn) and when the pause routine ends (Key4MusicOn), and stopped at a level's start (LevelStartSound, which also plays an effect) and when key 4 is pressed (Key4MusicOff). The 48K beeper is cut off at its three routines.
$5B00 c FramePlay ; page 4 in, one frame of the engine (EnginePlay), page 0 back; DI, every register but HL kept
> Called from the game's interrupt handler through PlayAtA9E5, PlayAtA581, PlayAtA9F7 and PlayAtAB03. Leaves interrupts off (the handler enables them itself). AF, DE, BC, IX, IY kept; the engine may change HL.
$5B01 ; AF, DE, BC, IX, IY kept
$5B08 ; page 4: the engine
$5B12 ; page 0: the game
$5B21 c PlayAtA9E5 ; the handler at $A9E4 (the menu's): a frame of the engine, then the LD HL,IntFlag it lost
> Reached by CALL PlayAtA9E5 at IntMenuSite, which held LD HL,IntFlag (3 bytes).
$5B28 c PlayAtA581 ; the handler tail at $A581: a frame of the engine, its POP BC: POP DE: POP HL, back to its POP AF
> Reached by JP PlayAtA581 at IntTailSite.
$5B31 c PlayAtA9F7 ; the main handler's work: DI, its PUSH IX: PUSH IY, a frame of the engine, on at IntPlayRest
> Reached by JP PlayAtA9F7 (and a NOP) at IntPlaySite.
$5B3C c PlayAtAB03 ; the main handler's other path ($AA00 jumps to $AB03): a frame of the engine, its POP IY: POP IX, on at IntEndRest
> Reached by JP PlayAtAB03 (and a NOP) at IntEndSite. The work from $A9FB always ends here (it runs to $AB03 or jumps there from $AA00), so the main handler (entered at $A9ED) steps the engine twice an interrupt: in c1 $A9ED ran 3221 times and PlayAtA9F7 and PlayAtAB03 3220 times each, while PlayAtA9E5 (2550) and PlayAtA581 (1403) step it once. The in-play handler is taken only every second TV frame (a pass ends with the next frame's interrupt already gone), so the in-play music and effects keep the menus' rate: w1 has 9701 engine steps in 9700 frames, z128A's r3 75 988 in 76 003 (docs/09-sound.md 9.8, docs/04-game-loop.md 4.3).
$5B46 c ClearThenMusic ; CALL ClearScreen, then MusicOn
> Replaces CALL ClearScreen at ClearSite1, ClearSite2 and ClearSite3 (the menu's and the game over's screen clears).
$5B49 MusicOn ; the main loop's CALL $AFB0 (at $B200) becomes CALL MusicOn; A = $5B (not 0): the music on
$5B50 c MusicSwitch ; A = 0: the music stopped; else stopped and started again from its beginning
> Input: A. Pages 4 in, calls EngineMusicOff, then EngineMusicOn when A is not 0 (A is kept in the operand of the LD A at MusicFlag, self-modifying: page 4's paging needs A), pages 0 back and enables interrupts. Used by the stubs too (HookSelections, HookScreenWipe: A = 0).
$5B54 ; page 4
$5B5E MusicFlag ; LD A,the switch (the operand written above)
$5B64 ; page 0
$5B6D c LevelStartSound ; a level's start: the music off, the engine's effect $C9A5, then LevelSetUp
> Replaces CALL LevelSetUp at LevelSite (in $B023). Pushes LevelSetUp's address and calls HookSound with L = $A5: HookSound's last POP HL takes this routine's return address and its RET goes to LevelSetUp, whose RET returns to $B023's caller's place after the CALL: the effect starts, then LevelSetUp runs as before (HL is LevelSetUp's own).
$5B71 ; LevelSetUp, under HookSound's return address
$5B7B c Key4MusicOff ; key 4 in play: the music off, then the game's routine Key4Routine
> Replaces the operand of CALL Z,Key4Routine at Key4Site. Key4Routine ends at Key4End, patched to Key4MusicOn.
$5B82 c Key4MusicOn ; the end of Key4Routine: its LD (PauseState),A, then MusicOn
> Reached by JP Key4MusicOn at Key4End; MusicOn's RET (MusicSwitch's) returns from Key4Routine.
$5B87 c GlueInstall ; the patches of the 48K game for the 128K (called once by block 2's set-up)
> In order: CALL PlayAtA9E5 at IntMenuSite; JP PlayAtA581 at IntTailSite; JP Key4MusicOn at Key4End; JP PlayAtA9F7 at IntPlaySite and JP PlayAtAB03 at IntEndSite, each followed by a NOP; BeeperTone's DI made a NOP; CALL ClearThenMusic at ClearSite3, ClearSite2, ClearSite1; CALL LevelStartSound at LevelSite; CALL Z,Key4MusicOff at Key4Site; RET at BeeperPlay and BeeperSound. The music is not started here: the first screen clear starts it.
$5B92 ; JP: the handler tail, the pause's end, the main handler's two places
$5BB8 ; NOPs after the two JPs, the beeper tone's DI off
$5BC2 ; the screen clears call ClearThenMusic
$5BCE ; the level's start, key 4
$5BDA ; the beeper's player and sound start: RET
